The "All products" and "Bundles" headings on the products page are now in capitals, 16px, with 0.08em letter spacing.

The change is one rule added to the Products block in `site/css/pages.css`:

```css
.page-products .section-title {
  font-size: 16px;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
}
```

Other pages use the same `section-title` class, so I limited the rule to the products page. Section headings elsewhere are unchanged.

**Checked in a browser:**
- On the products page, both headings show as 16px, capitals and 1.28px letter spacing (0.08em) at desktop width and at a 400px mobile width. Without the new rule, mobile would have shrunk them to 21px.
- The home page section heading is still 24px and not capitalised.
- All 16 functional tests pass.

`.idea` and `.vscode` folders now show as untracked in git status. I didn't create them, so I left them alone.

STATUS: DONE

